name: legendary
after: 29-proving-this-machine
intro: The last one before the machine itself falls. Hints cost nothing here --
intro: see how far you get without them. Every stage uses something from an
intro: earlier level, and none of them fit on one line comfortably.
---
setup: Each level under /usr/share/learn/levels declares the commands it drills
setup: on ref: lines. You want the commands that appear across the most
setup: separate levels -- the load-bearing ones the whole curriculum leans on.
q: print the five most frequently drilled commands with their counts, most first
a: sed -n 's/^ref: //p' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -n 5
ref: uniq
cmp: ref
hint: uniq -c needs sorted input first, or it only dedupes adjacent runs
---
setup: A ref exists under /usr/share/learn/ref for every shipped command; the
setup: levels drill only some. There is no comm here and ash has no process
setup: substitution, so you difference two lists with grep instead.
q: write the commands drilled in /usr/share/learn/levels to /tmp/taught, sorted and deduplicated, one per line
a: sed -n 's/^ref: //p' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sort -u > /tmp/taught
a: grep -h '^ref: ' /usr/share/learn/levels/* | sed 's/^ref: //' | sort -u > /tmp/taught
ref: sort
hint: redirect the sorted, deduplicated list straight into the file
---
setup: /tmp/taught now holds one drilled command per line.
q: print every command documented in /usr/share/learn/ref but absent from /tmp/taught
a: ls /usr/share/learn/ref | grep -vxF -f /tmp/taught
a: ls /usr/share/learn/ref | grep -vxFf /tmp/taught
ref: grep
hint: -f reads patterns from a file; -x anchors each to a whole line; -v inverts
---
setup: Prove nothing in /usr/share/learn/ref was altered since you built it: one
setup: digest over every file's contents at once.
q: print a single sha256 digest covering every file in /usr/share/learn/ref
a: cat /usr/share/learn/ref/* | sha256sum
a: find /usr/share/learn/ref -type f | sort | xargs cat | sha256sum
ref: sha256sum
hint: concatenate every file into one stream before hashing it once
---
setup: The final question. /proc/mounts, field 4 the comma-separated options.
q: print each mount option in /proc/mounts that appears on more than one filesystem, with its count
a: awk '{print $4}' /proc/mounts | tr ',' '\n' | sort | uniq -c | awk '$1>1'
ref: awk
cmp: ref
hint: split the comma list onto separate lines before you sort and count
